      "page_markdown": "documents/G186.md#page-41",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "text": "For most organizations, the budget cycle controls change in the organization. Pragmatically, the EA team will be aligned to the budget cycle. Figure 4-1 shows a timeline view, depicting an alignment of key decisions made during a business cycle and the purpose architectures. EA for Strategy, Portfolio, and Project need to be completed before key milestones for budget decisions are made. EA for Solution Delivery is a continuous operation around budget control. The key takeaway is architecture before the decision. If you are trapped trying to architect after the decision, see Section 11.2.1.",
